{
 "formula": "P = (Radixite + 2*Metal + 3*VehicleParts) / 100, weights from the DeveloperSettings::GameBalance::UnitCosts note that metal is twice and vehicle parts three times as rare as radixite. raw = (Base + K*P) * (clamp(TrainingTime, 12, 45) / 20)^0.15 (the time factor is only a mild modifier, 0.93x at 12 s to 1.13x at 45 s, so supply is resource-dominated), with Base/K per category: infantry 2/0.9, team weapons 2/0.65, vehicles 6/1.0, aircraft 6/1.0; economy units (harvester, nomadic trucks) use 2 + 0.6*P with no time factor. The per-category Base is a fixed per-unit overhead that lifts cheap vehicles (an Sd.Kfz. 250 costs about as much as a rifle squad in resources but is a durable vehicle), and the lower team-weapon K reflects that crew-served guns cost more resources than their mobility is worth in a defensive start army. Rounding: raw <= 10 rounds to an integer (minimum 1), 10-30 to an integer, above 30 to a multiple of 5. Overrides: every faction HQ = 0, harvester floor 5, Metal Vault priced from its intended 250 Radixite + 125 Metal. Variants get their own value only when clearly stronger or weaker than base (x0.80-x1.20 of base, re-rounded); unlisted variants cost the base value.",
 "suggested_defaults": {
  "SupplyBudget": 100,
  "SlotCount": 12,
  "reasoning": "Slots count every unit including the HQ (HQ costs 0 supply). Breakthrough example, 89 supply in 11 slots: HQ Truck (0), Panzer IV H (21), Panzer IV G (16), Panzer Grenadiers (12), 2x JagerTrupp 98K (4), Scavengers (4), Sdkfz. 250 (8), Sdkfz. 250/37 (8), Pak 38 (7), PanzerI Harvester (5). Heavy-tank opener, 89 supply in 9 slots: HQ Truck (0), Tiger H1 (30), Panzer IV H (21), Panzer Grenadiers (12), 2x JagerTrupp 98K (4), Scavengers (4), Sdkfz. 250 (8), GrW 42 80mm Mortar (6). Strike Division example, 92 supply in 10 slots: HQ Truck (0), Panther D (29), Stug III (13), Panzer Grenadiers (12), 2x JagerTrupp 98K (4), Puma (10), Sdkfz. 251 Transport (8), Pak 38 (7), PanzerI Harvester (5). A King Tiger (40) or Maus/E100 (60) is affordable but takes 40-60% of the budget, so a super-heavy start is a real trade against breadth. The 12-slot cap binds first for armies of 4-supply squads (it stops a 25-squad Jager swarm), the 100 budget binds first for armour-heavy armies."
 },
